<exercisegroup cols="2" xml:id="exercisegroup-vector-geom-verify-triangle">
<title>Triangle inequality</title>

<introduction><p>
	In each case,
	verify that <m> \uvec{u} </m> and <m> \uvec{v} </m> satisfy the <xref ref="theorem-vector-geom-triangle-ineq" text="title" />.
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} </m> and <m> \uvec{v} </m> from <xref ref="exercise-vector-geom-compute-angle-R2-1" text="type-local" />. </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<p>
		<m> \unorm{u} = \sqrt{29} </m> and <m> \unorm{v} = \sqrt{41} </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} = \sqrt{29} + \sqrt{41} \approx 11.67 </m>.
		</p>

		<p>
		<m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} = (10, -6) </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u + v} = \sqrt{136} \approx 11.79 </m>.
		</p>

		<p> Hence it is true that <m> \norm{\uvec{u} + \uvec{v}} \le \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} </m>. </p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} </m> and <m> \uvec{v} </m> from <xref ref="exercise-vector-geom-compute-angle-R2-2" text="type-local" />. </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<p>
		<m> \unorm{u} = \sqrt{41} </m> and <m> \unorm{v} = 5 </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} = \sqrt{41} + 5 \approx 11.40 </m>.
		</p>

		<p>
		<m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} = (7, 1) </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u + v} = 5 \sqrt{2} \approx 7.07 </m>.
		</p>

		<p> Hence it is true that <m> \norm{\uvec{u} + \uvec{v}} \le \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} </m>. </p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} </m> and <m> \uvec{v} </m> from <xref ref="exercise-vector-geom-compute-angle-R3-1" text="type-local" />. </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<p>
		<m> \unorm{u} = \sqrt{61} </m> and <m> \unorm{v} = 2 \sqrt{2} </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} = \sqrt{61} + 2 \sqrt{2} \approx 10.64 </m>.
		</p>

		<p>
		<m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} = (6, -1, -6) </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u + v} = \sqrt{73} \approx 8.54 </m>.
		</p>

		<p> Hence it is true that <m> \norm{\uvec{u} + \uvec{v}} \le \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} </m>. </p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} </m> and <m> \uvec{v} </m> from <xref ref="exercise-vector-geom-compute-angle-R3-2" text="type-local" />. </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<p>
		<m> \unorm{u} = \sqrt{46} </m> and <m> \unorm{v} = 5 \sqrt{2} </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} = \sqrt{46} + 5 \sqrt{2} \approx 13.85 </m>.
		</p>

		<p>
		<m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} = (-2, 4, -2) </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u + v} = 2 \sqrt{6} \approx 4.90 </m>.
		</p>

		<p> Hence it is true that <m> \norm{\uvec{u} + \uvec{v}} \le \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} </m>. </p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} </m> and <m> \uvec{v} </m> from <xref ref="exercise-vector-geom-compute-angle-R4" text="type-local" />. </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<p>
		<m> \unorm{u} = \sqrt{74} </m> and <m> \unorm{v} = \sqrt{19} </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} = \sqrt{74} + \sqrt{19} \approx 12.96 </m>.
		</p>

		<p>
		<m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} = (7, -1, -3, 2) </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u + v} = 3 \sqrt{7} \approx 7.94 </m>.
		</p>

		<p> Hence it is true that <m> \norm{\uvec{u} + \uvec{v}} \le \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} </m>. </p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} </m> and <m> \uvec{v} </m> from <xref ref="exercise-vector-geom-compute-angle-R5" text="type-local" />. </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<p>
		<m> \unorm{u} = 2 \sqrt{14} </m> and <m> \unorm{v} = \sqrt{97} </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} = 2 \sqrt{14} + \sqrt{97} \approx 17.33 </m>.
		</p>

		<p>
		<m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} = (7, 4, -1, 10, -5) </m>,
		so <m> \unorm{u + v} = \sqrt{191} \approx 13.82 </m>.
		</p>

		<p> Hence it is true that <m> \norm{\uvec{u} + \uvec{v}} \le \unorm{u} + \unorm{v} </m>. </p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
